  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "Watch this speaker cone. A changing electrical signal will make it move. Inside, a coil sits in the field of a permanent magnet. The audio signal sends alternating current through that coil. The current reverses, so the magnetic force reverses too. The coil pulls the cone inward, then pushes it outward. Follow the cone, not the waveform. As the cone moves out, it compresses the air in front. As it moves back, it leaves a region of lower pressure. Those pressure variations travel outward as sound. Electrical variations become mechanical motion, and motion becomes sound.",
